t it is incredibly slow  if you plug in your lightning cable into  the bank itself you will have a full  charge  in one hour and 15 minutes or two hours  if it is also charging your phone at the  same time but if you plug the cable into  your phone  it will take five hours to reverse  wirelessly charge  the battery bank and the other thing is  reverse wireless charging won't  work if your phone is charging i only  saw it kick in once my phone stopped  charging  so that five hours is with a fully  charged iphone  that means it will take you seven hours  to fully charge both your phone  and the bank reversely if you have a 20  watt  charger into your iphone 12 compared to  3 hours and 15 minutes  if you just decide to plug it into the  pack itself and attach your phone  in addition you can't use anything but  an iphone 12 series phone  to reverse wirelessly charge this pack  so if you have a wireless charging pad  a magsafe puck or even one of the three  in one magsafe stands that have that  little base  you cannot use it to charge this you  will start having to use a lightning  cable like you did before  and that's not even the worst or most  annoying thing about it  let's get into the charging performance  and major limitations  for my testing i use an iphone 12 which  is by far the most popular new  iphone but the 12 pro should charge  exactly the same since it has the same  battery  and i will also comment on the 12 mini  and the 12 for max in just a little bit  i made sure the iphone 12 was completely  drained and attached each battery  to see how long they would take to turn  your phone back on  and the name brands were a fair bit  quicker compared to the third party  options  after 15 minutes apple's magsafe hit  nine percent  better than blue mini which only hit six  percent but slightly behind anchor at 10  and kickstand managed 12 at the 30  minute mark  all chargers about double their charge  rate with the blue mini hitting  13 max eighth at 18 anchors still higher  at 19 and kickstand at 23  so as you can see we were right in our  first video about this charger  when you're using it as a wireless  powered pack it provides nowhere near 15  watt max safe speeds  which is the biggest reason so many of  us were waiting for  and willing to pay extra for it i tested  all of them using an  app that actually measures how much  wattage is captured by the battery  and apple's is slightly lower than  anker's better than blue mini  but still behind other third options  that can charge wirelessly at up to 7.5  watts  let's skip over 45 minutes and jump  straight to the one hour mark  and apple's pack hits 36 percent the  blue mini is slower at 28  and kickstand is much higher at 42  but the other chargers have another  advantage jumping into the one and a  half hour mark which is where wired fast  charging would have fully charged the  iphone 12  apple's magsafe pack hit 53 and just  15 minutes after that the pack was  completely drained  charging our iphone to 57 at that time  inger was slightly ahead but still had  power  and kickstand reached a much higher 68  our smallest and slowest charger reached  the same amount as magsafe  about 15 minutes later but it kept going  until 68  and the other two kept charging for  another 30 minutes  until they hit 87 and 95  so apple's charger is only faster than  the much smaller and cheaper blue mini  charger  but the charge capacity is far lower  than all the third-party options  apple's pack is also more efficient but  doesn't really matter if it can only  provide 57  charge with an iphone 12 or 44  with the 12 pro max and even the mini  with a tiny battery only charges  79 of it now i know that some of you  will say that you don't need a full  charge from it  you just want to maintain your iphone's  battery while you're using it  and just pull from the external one kind  of like you did with apple's old battery  cases  well that's the last disappointment this  thing is very sensitive to heat  maybe because apple is being sensitive  to battery longevity  or maybe because heat will make the tiny  battery in it die super quickly  and give you barely any charge although  the previous charge percentages were  when i wasn't using the phone and it was  in a cool room  when you're using it and there's  anything that is pushing the phone the  battery won't charge  even though the logo shows up in my  previous video i  shared that the battery pack wasn't  charging when i was gaming and the  battery drained from 100 to 90  and 30 minutes of gaming while anchors  held the battery  i did the same test again but i started  at 50  battery to make sure that there weren't  any charging limitations  and after 30 minutes of call of duty the  battery dropped to 36 percent  and the pack barely changed in its  capacity anker  kept the battery at the same charge and  the phone only lost two percent when  using the blue mini charger  that has a slower charge speed this  isn't with gaming  exclusively other tougher apps caused  the maxi pack to stop  charging as well and yesterday i was out  on the boat  and the battery pack was not charging my  phone even though it wasn't super hot  out  and there was also a breeze going now i  understand battery longevity but if i  were to plug a cable into my phone  it would still charge during these times  even  if that meant that it would get hotter  so taking everything into account  this thing cost a hundred bucks and has  way too many limitations compared to  third-party options  that provide more charge are way more  flexible and smaller  and cheaper so basically because of this  i'm returning  two out of the three packs that i bought  the two that work for my own personal  use  and i'm gonna be keeping this one in the  office just because i need to for future  references  and for those of you out there i would  say most people should not buy one  as well the only two groups that i think  might still want to buy it are those who  don't care about performance  at all unless you want to buy something  that is named brand that they know that  will last a long time  but personally with that said i'd rather  use this and maybe in a year or two have  to buy a new one  and it'd still be way less than this or  those of you guys that don't  yet have a wireless charging pad and  you're gonna use this for dual purpose  both as a wireless pass-through charging  pad and at the same time an extra bank  as well  in that case that does make it a better  value but  overall i am just not so thrilled with  apple's pack but you guys let me know  your thoughts down in the comments  section below  click that circle above if you guys  enjoyed this video you want to see more  like it that will help us reach our goal  of a million subscribers before the end  of the year this is max and i will see  you  in the next video

